{"acceptedResponses":["E"],"answer":"E","bank":"amc","batch":"B","choiceOrder":["A","B","C","D","E"],"choices":{"A":"\\(30\\)","B":"\\(\\dfrac{400}{11}\\)","C":"\\(\\dfrac{75}{2}\\)","D":"\\(40\\)","E":"\\(\\dfrac{300}{7}\\)"},"choicesType":"text","domain":[],"editorialNote":"","figureSources":{},"id":"2014_AMC_12B_Q03","knowledgeGraph":{"assessedIds":["cnm_p184"],"contentHash":"e6c6e8a0992a20fcd837192099954917519da02dc1db98ccbdacdc306f66f197","flags":[],"reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"known-fraction-of-trip","label":"Divide by the paved fraction","methodDirectNodeIds":{"known-fraction-of-trip":["cnm_p183"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p183"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"total-distance-equation","label":"Linear distance equation","methodDirectNodeIds":{"total-distance-equation":["cnm_045","cnm_044"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_045","cnm_044"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p174","cnm_p183"],"id":"find-paved-fraction","label":"Find the fraction traveled on pavement","methodDirectNodeIds":{"find-paved-fraction":["cnm_p184"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p184","cnm_p174","cnm_p183"]}],"status":"mapped","supportIds":["cnm_p174","cnm_p183"],"version":"1.0.0"},"level":"AMC 12","number":3,"question":"Randy drove the first third of his trip on a gravel road, the next \\(20\\) miles on pavement, and the remaining one-fifth on a dirt road. In miles, how long was Randy’s trip?","questionType":"text","rejectedAnswers":[],"responseType":"choice","schemaVersion":"3.0","skill":[],"solution":"The gravel and dirt portions occupy \\(\\tfrac13\\) and \\(\\tfrac15\\) of the whole trip. The paved portion is everything left over, so it accounts for\n\\[\n1-\\frac13-\\frac15\n=\\frac{15-5-3}{15}\n=\\frac7{15}\n\\]\nof the total distance.\n\nSince this \\(\\tfrac7{15}\\) portion is 20 miles, the whole trip is\n\\[\n20\\div\\frac7{15}\n=20\\cdot\\frac{15}{7}\n=\\frac{300}{7}\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{300}{7}}\\) miles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).","solutionA